(4091074, 581699, 53814, '<td valign="top">Great job nailing the DOF and bokeh on this one, Ann. Congratulations on capturing your first ribbon, I expect you will get many more.</td>', 'Great job nailing the DOF and bokeh on this one, Ann. Congratulations on capturing your first ribbon, I expect you will get many more.', '2007-09-15 02:20:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(4091191, 580787, 52549, '<td valign="top">Rita, don''t feel like a fraud - FEEL HAPPY! This is a beautiful image and VERY worthy of a ribbon!</td>', 'Rita, don''t feel like a fraud - FEEL HAPPY! This is a beautiful image and VERY worthy of a ribbon!', '2007-09-15 03:54:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(4091327, 580846, 30791, '<td valign="top">great shot, it was one of my favorites. i wish this would have scored higher than it did, too many flower shots in this challenge.</td>', 'great shot, it was one of my favorites. i wish this would have scored higher than it did, too many flower shots in this challenge.', '2007-09-15 09:21:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(4091707, 581433, 24111, '<td valign="top">awesome!</td>', 'awesome!', '2007-09-15 13:03:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(4091740, 582130, 61818, '<td valign="top">Critique Club feedback -<br/> <br/>I think it is just a dandelion (a weed) so that''s probably why it got mowed down.<br/> <br/>Very nice bokeh behind the flower.  Does it enhance your subject?  I think so.  The flower is the one detailed thing on a see of little yellow dots of light.<br/> <br/>Focus on the flower could be much better. I would advise anyone to get the focus dead-on in camera.  PP sharpening is never as good.  Your shutter speed was a bit low here for the lens being used, that might have made all the difference.</td>', 'Critique Club feedback - I think it is just a dandelion (a weed) so that''s probably why it got mowed down. Very nice bokeh behind the flower.  Does it enhance your subject?  I think so.  The flower is the one detailed thing on a see of little yellow dots of light. Focus on the flower could be much better. I would advise anyone to get the focus dead-on in camera.  PP sharpening is never as good.  Your shutter speed was a bit low here for the lens being used, that might have made all the difference.', '2007-09-15 13:23:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(4091744, 582093, 61818, '<td valign="top">Critique Club feedback -<br/> <br/>Wow it looks like mothra from the godzilla movies lol.<br/> <br/>Great capture, you really got some good focus on that bug and that''s not easy to do.<br/> <br/>Does the bokeh enhance the subject?  That I''m not so sure about.  Even with all the nice little circles of light, there is a lot of activity in the background and the dimly lit bug sort of disappears in the cacophony.</td>', 'Critique Club feedback - Wow it looks like mothra from the godzilla movies lol. Great capture, you really got some good focus on that bug and that''s not easy to do. Does the bokeh enhance the subject?  That I''m not so sure about.  Even with all the nice little circles of light, there is a lot of activity in the background and the dimly lit bug sort of disappears in the cacophony.', '2007-09-15 13:24:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(4091747, 581267, 61818, '<td valign="top">Critique Club feedback -<br/> <br/>Bug shots are hard to score well with simply from the large numbers of them and the bar being raised pretty high.  I think were the spider in crisp focus here this would have done better.  Also you could try cropping it differently to see if there is a way to compose the shot which would give it more impact.<br/> <br/>Bokeh?  I''m in the camp that bokeh is those little circles of light, but even going with the ''out of focus areas of the photo'' definition - I think there''s still a lot of detail in the background here that doesn''t enhance your subject and sort of makes for a busy shot.</td>', 'Critique Club feedback - Bug shots are hard to score well with simply from the large numbers of them and the bar being raised pretty high.  I think were the spider in crisp focus here this would have done better.  Also you could try cropping it differently to see if there is a way to compose the shot which would give it more impact. Bokeh?  I''m in the camp that bokeh is those little circles of light, but even going with the ''out of focus areas of the photo'' definition - I think there''s still a lot of detail in the background here that doesn''t enhance your subject and sort of makes for a busy shot.', '2007-09-15 13:27:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(4091749, 581586, 61818, '<td valign="top">Critique Club feedback -<br/> <br/>The out of focus background is pleasing to look at, but this would have scored much higher were the bug itself in focus.</td>', 'Critique Club feedback - The out of focus background is pleasing to look at, but this would have scored much higher were the bug itself in focus.', '2007-09-15 13:28:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(4091751, 581930, 61818, '<td valign="top">Critique Club feedback -<br/> <br/>The cage lines aresort of distracting, but I actually find myself liking how they break up the background.  nice bokeh.  The angle this was shot from and the composition of the shot probably kept the score down a little bit.  The lighting is nice though, I like how it highlights the bird''s face.</td>', 'Critique Club feedback - The cage lines aresort of distracting, but I actually find myself liking how they break up the background.  nice bokeh.  The angle this was shot from and the composition of the shot probably kept the score down a little bit.  The lighting is nice though, I like how it highlights the bird''s face.', '2007-09-15 13:30:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(4091753, 580800, 61818, '<td valign="top">Critique Club feedback -<br/> <br/>The bokeh is nice and the way it comes off as dim reflections of the main subject does enhance the subject in my opinion.<br/> <br/>The subject itself would look better were it more in focus (narrower aperture) and there might be better crops/compositions that would give the overall photo more impact.</td>', 'Critique Club feedback - The bokeh is nice and the way it comes off as dim reflections of the main subject does enhance the subject in my opinion. The subject itself would look better were it more in focus (narrower aperture) and there might be better crops/compositions that would give the overall photo more impact.', '2007-09-15 13:31:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(4091761, 582462, 61818, '<td valign="top">Critique Club feedback -<br/> <br/>I''m afraid that by any definition I don''t see any bokeh in this shot, and I think I''m not alone in that perception. Google ''bokeh'' and have a look at the other images in this challenge and you will be well prepared for the next bokeh challenge.</td>', 'Critique Club feedback - I''m afraid that by any definition I don''t see any bokeh in this shot, and I think I''m not alone in that perception. Google ''bokeh'' and have a look at the other images in this challenge and you will be well prepared for the next bokeh challenge.', '2007-09-15 13:36:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(4091770, 582411, 61818, '<td valign="top">Critique Club feedback -<br/> <br/>I think with the challenge being to have bokeh enhance your subject, entering a photo with no subject at all is sort of missing the point.<br/> <br/>Consider always submitting shots at the full dimensions allowed by the challenge.  I think I might actually like this abstract, but it is so small I can''t really digest it.</td>', 'Critique Club feedback - I think with the challenge being to have bokeh enhance your subject, entering a photo with no subject at all is sort of missing the point. Consider always submitting shots at the full dimensions allowed by the challenge.  I think I might actually like this abstract, but it is so small I can''t really digest it.', '2007-09-15 13:41:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(4091773, 581732, 30982, '<td valign="top">A rather ho-hum score for what I see as an elegantly presented play of color and form.  I very much appreciate the composition in halves - very well handled in my opinion.</td>', 'A rather ho-hum score for what I see as an elegantly presented play of color and form.  I very much appreciate the composition in halves - very well handled in my opinion.', '2007-09-15 13:41:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(4091775, 579706, 61818, '<td valign="top">Critique Club feedback -<br/> <br/>not a lot of excitement here, but as far as sticking to the challenge I think you really nailed it.  The bokeh really does enhance the subject.  The logo of the bike popsout of the image, and then the bokeh behind still leaves enough impression of the rest of the bike to complete the image.<br/> <br/>Nice job!</td>', 'Critique Club feedback - not a lot of excitement here, but as far as sticking to the challenge I think you really nailed it.  The bokeh really does enhance the subject.  The logo of the bike popsout of the image, and then the bokeh behind still leaves enough impression of the rest of the bike to complete the image. Nice job!', '2007-09-15 13:42:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(4091778, 582299, 61818, '<td valign="top">Critique Club feedback -<br/> <br/>Very nice.  Has an (dare I say it) impressionist feel to it. The bokeh perfectly complements and enhances the subject.  Nice lighting too, I like how the subject is highlighted.</td>', 'Critique Club feedback - Very nice.  Has an (dare I say it) impressionist feel to it. The bokeh perfectly complements and enhances the subject.  Nice lighting too, I like how the subject is highlighted.', '2007-09-15 13:43:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(4091781, 578872, 61818, '<td valign="top">Critique Club feedback -<br/> <br/>The oof areas certainly enhance the subject and give a strong sense of depth to the image.  The rope itself is overexposed.  I like the angle you shot (or cropped) this on as well.  Nice details on the hands.</td>', 'Critique Club feedback - The oof areas certainly enhance the subject and give a strong sense of depth to the image.  The rope itself is overexposed.  I like the angle you shot (or cropped) this on as well.  Nice details on the hands.', '2007-09-15 13:44:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(4091790, 582510, 61818, '<td valign="top">Critique Club feedback -<br/> <br/>As a fellow butterfly submitter to this challenge, how can I avoid saying great subject for the challenge! lol<br/> <br/>Very nice bokeh here and I think it enhances the subject in a general sense.  However, I shot a bunch of these moth looking furry sort of butterflies which are so pale in color.  My own opinion and the reason they never made it out of lightroom - they just look so damned boring.  No colors and they are very difficult to make out detail on as they are so pale.<br/> <br/>Overall, nice stuff!</td>', 'Critique Club feedback - As a fellow butterfly submitter to this challenge, how can I avoid saying great subject for the challenge! lol Very nice bokeh here and I think it enhances the subject in a general sense.  However, I shot a bunch of these moth looking furry sort of butterflies which are so pale in color.  My own opinion and the reason they never made it out of lightroom - they just look so damned boring.  No colors and they are very difficult to make out detail on as they are so pale. Overall, nice stuff!', '2007-09-15 13:46:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(4091794, 582197, 61818, '<td valign="top">Critique Club feedback -<br/> <br/>I''m not sure what you mean by great lighting.  Certainly this is brightly lit.<br/> <br/>The glare spots on the plant and the harsh shadows being cast are generally the antithesis of great lighting.  Lighting should complement the subject and provide no distractions.<br/> <br/>I am wondering if your camera was set on auto mode here?  Very odd combination of settings and partly responsible for the shot being a bit overexposed and an aperture which kept an awful lot of detail in the background at the expense of more bokeh.<br/> <br/>Don''t think the bokeh here, what there is of it, really enhances the subject.  The subject is so pronounced in the frame that the background really doesn''t get  much play, and thus no chance to really add to the shot overall.</td>', 'Critique Club feedback - I''m not sure what you mean by great lighting.  Certainly this is brightly lit. The glare spots on the plant and the harsh shadows being cast are generally the antithesis of great lighting.  Lighting should complement the subject and provide no distractions. I am wondering if your camera was set on auto mode here?  Very odd combination of settings and partly responsible for the shot being a bit overexposed and an aperture which kept an awful lot of detail in the background at the expense of more bokeh. Don''t think the bokeh here, what there is of it, really enhances the subject.  The subject is so pronounced in the frame that the background really doesn''t get  much play, and thus no chance to really add to the shot overall.', '2007-09-15 13:49:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(4091801, 581738, 61818, '<td valign="top">Critique Club feedback -<br/> <br/>Nice bokeh which does complement the subject (how could it not when it is part of the subject after all? lol).<br/> <br/>Sharper focus on the center part of the flower would work better here, and possible a different composition getting the center of the flower out of the center of the frame.</td>', 'Critique Club feedback - Nice bokeh which does complement the subject (how could it not when it is part of the subject after all? lol). Sharper focus on the center part of the flower would work better here, and possible a different composition getting the center of the flower out of the center of the frame.', '2007-09-15 13:54:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(4091808, 581892, 61818, '<td valign="top">Critique Club feedback -<br/> <br/>The bokeh here does providea nice background which complements the subject and sets it apart.  Focus on the bird could be much better, and you could try different crops on this to compose the scene for more impact.</td>', 'Critique Club feedback - The bokeh here does providea nice background which complements the subject and sets it apart.  Focus on the bird could be much better, and you could try different crops on this to compose the scene for more impact.', '2007-09-15 13:56:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(4091810, 582075, 30982, '<td valign="top">I like this use of bokeh.  While the common approach is to use flowers, I think people-bokeh is very effective when shooting people.  Wonder if people-bokeh also works for flowers...</td>', 'I like this use of bokeh.  While the common approach is to use flowers, I think people-bokeh is very effective when shooting people.  Wonder if people-bokeh also works for flowers...', '2007-09-15 13:56:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(4091811, 580473, 61818, '<td valign="top">Critique Club feedback -<br/> <br/>This is an excellent image of a knife. Unfortunately it pretty much completely misses the point of the challenge.<br/> <br/>Great details on those water droplets.  I hope to see your work in future challenges.</td>', 'Critique Club feedback - This is an excellent image of a knife. Unfortunately it pretty much completely misses the point of the challenge. Great details on those water droplets.  I hope to see your work in future challenges.', '2007-09-15 13:57:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(4091815, 580579, 61818, '<td valign="top">Critique Club feedback -<br/> <br/>The bokeh here is interesting and is an integral part of the shot.  I''m not sure this was the best choice for b/w though, as the whole shot seems to fade into a blur of light gray as you look at it.</td>', 'Critique Club feedback - The bokeh here is interesting and is an integral part of the shot.  I''m not sure this was the best choice for b/w though, as the whole shot seems to fade into a blur of light gray as you look at it.', '2007-09-15 13:58:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(4091817, 582140, 61818, '<td valign="top">Critique Club feedback -<br/> <br/>First thing I thought when I looked at this is ''whitebalance is off''.  Then I read that you adjusted it, so I''m thinking it might be worth practicing in that regard  some more.<br/> <br/>Bokeh here is nice and the distant glimmers of additional flowers do enhance the main subject.  Just a bit less detail back there would work even better imo.<br/> <br/>Good job!</td>', 'Critique Club feedback - First thing I thought when I looked at this is ''whitebalance is off''.  Then I read that you adjusted it, so I''m thinking it might be worth practicing in that regard  some more. Bokeh here is nice and the distant glimmers of additional flowers do enhance the main subject.  Just a bit less detail back there would work even better imo. Good job!', '2007-09-15 14:00:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(4091819, 580943, 61818, '<td valign="top">Critique Club feedback -<br/> <br/>This was quite nice and certainly met the challenge.  It''s score and placing were both well deserved - what more is there to say?</td>', 'Critique Club feedback - This was quite nice and certainly met the challenge.  It''s score and placing were both well deserved - what more is there to say?', '2007-09-15 14:02:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(4091820, 580954, 61818, '<td valign="top">Critique Club feedback -<br/> <br/>I really like the flare and the overall lighting is superb.  had you gotten the milkweed in crisp focus, this shot would really pop.</td>', 'Critique Club feedback - I really like the flare and the overall lighting is superb.  had you gotten the milkweed in crisp focus, this shot would really pop.', '2007-09-15 14:03:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(4091826, 579706, 61961, '<td valign="top">I would have liked to see more bokeh fill the background, but I was drawn to this photo because it stood out from all the nature photos.  I like the composition, there is good foreground detail and the blue of the bike is pretty (the orange bit is nice, too).  Overall I think you did a fine job.  I gave this an "8."</td>', 'I would have liked to see more bokeh fill the background, but I was drawn to this photo because it stood out from all the nature photos.  I like the composition, there is good foreground detail and the blue of the bike is pretty (the orange bit is nice, too).  Overall I think you did a fine job.  I gave this an "8."', '2007-09-15 14:06:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(4091827, 582056, 61818, '<td valign="top">Critique Club feedback -<br/> <br/>I think the bokeh works well here even if the background is still a bit heavy on detail.<br/> <br/>The flower appears to float on that sea of green.  Flower itself could be a bit crisper.<br/> <br/>Overall, very nice shot.</td>', 'Critique Club feedback - I think the bokeh works well here even if the background is still a bit heavy on detail. The flower appears to float on that sea of green.  Flower itself could be a bit crisper. Overall, very nice shot.', '2007-09-15 14:06:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(4091832, 582562, 61818, '<td valign="top">Critique Club feedback -<br/> <br/>Bokeh does a nice job of popping the girl out of the background.<br/> <br/>Last minute edit responsible for cropping her knee off?  That''s really the only big negative here.   I do like the pose.  Image could be a bit sharper overall.</td>', 'Critique Club feedback - Bokeh does a nice job of popping the girl out of the background. Last minute edit responsible for cropping her knee off?  That''s really the only big negative here.   I do like the pose.  Image could be a bit sharper overall.', '2007-09-15 14:08:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(4091844, 581441, 61818, '<td valign="top">Critique Club feedback -<br/> <br/>The bokeh doesa nicejob hereof causing the model to pop out of the image.<br/> <br/>Composition here is a bit odd, could try cropping so the face is either prominent in the scene or located elsewhere in the frame.<br/> <br/>Model''s expression is... odd.  Normally I say ''well what can you do about that model'', but here I se eit''s your kid so there''s no excuse! ;)<br/> <br/>To be honest I''m not sure why this score a 4.9.  It''s not the most exciting image, but it certainly isn''t that bad (and doesn''t merit ten 3 votes by any stretch of the imagination).<br/> <br/>Good luck!</td>', 'Critique Club feedback - The bokeh doesa nicejob hereof causing the model to pop out of the image. Composition here is a bit odd, could try cropping so the face is either prominent in the scene or located elsewhere in the frame. Model''s expression is... odd.  Normally I say ''well what can you do about that model'', but here I se eit''s your kid so there''s no excuse! ;) To be honest I''m not sure why this score a 4.9.  It''s not the most exciting image, but it certainly isn''t that bad (and doesn''t merit ten 3 votes by any stretch of the imagination). Good luck!', '2007-09-15 14:15:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(4091846, 582533, 61818, '<td valign="top">Critique Club feedback -<br/> <br/>Little bokeh here, and then only is the effects of focal fall-off counts as bokeh.  Composition is good, I like how you placed the snake''s head in the frame.  Overall this shot doesn''t really connect with the challenge too well.<br/> <br/></td>', 'Critique Club feedback - Little bokeh here, and then only is the effects of focal fall-off counts as bokeh.  Composition is good, I like how you placed the snake''s head in the frame.  Overall this shot doesn''t really connect with the challenge too well. ', '2007-09-15 14:17:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(4091849, 582254, 61818, '<td valign="top">Critique Club feedback -<br/> <br/>Nice bit of bokeh in the background.  I would concentrate on making sure your focus is accurate, trying different compositionts and add a bit of contrast to the shot to give the statue some life.</td>', 'Critique Club feedback - Nice bit of bokeh in the background.  I would concentrate on making sure your focus is accurate, trying different compositionts and add a bit of contrast to the shot to give the statue some life.', '2007-09-15 14:18:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(4091852, 582410, 61818, '<td valign="top">Critique Club feedback -<br/> <br/>Not sure that the bokeh enhances the subject here, but it does help define the overall scene.  Highlights on the fence are pretty overexposed.  20 minutes later the light might have been even better for this shot.<br/> <br/>Golden light falling on the girl''s face is very nice.  Getting all of her face in detail against the oof backgroundmight have enhanced that sense of being adrift in thought as the world moves on.</td>', 'Critique Club feedback - Not sure that the bokeh enhances the subject here, but it does help define the overall scene.  Highlights on the fence are pretty overexposed.  20 minutes later the light might have been even better for this shot. Golden light falling on the girl''s face is very nice.  Getting all of her face in detail against the oof backgroundmight have enhanced that sense of being adrift in thought as the world moves on.', '2007-09-15 14:20:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(4091856, 580607, 61818, '<td valign="top">Critique Club feedback -<br/> <br/>Not much bokeh here if any.  The lighting is not working in your favor here.  MAcro shots really need technical perfection to have impact.</td>', 'Critique Club feedback - Not much bokeh here if any.  The lighting is not working in your favor here.  MAcro shots really need technical perfection to have impact.', '2007-09-15 14:21:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(4091857, 582517, 61818, '<td valign="top">Critique Club feedback -<br/> <br/>Looks like bokeh to me and I think it enhances the subject, just in an unusual way.<br/> <br/>I like the narrow focus falling just on the bug and the overall green cast to the shot.  The details under the bug are also very nice.<br/> <br/>Could try playing with the composition on this to see if you can get it to pop a bit more, but overall this isn''t a bad shot at all.</td>', 'Critique Club feedback - Looks like bokeh to me and I think it enhances the subject, just in an unusual way. I like the narrow focus falling just on the bug and the overall green cast to the shot.  The details under the bug are also very nice. Could try playing with the composition on this to see if you can get it to pop a bit more, but overall this isn''t a bad shot at all.', '2007-09-15 14:22:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(4092016, 580787, 17513, '<td valign="top">stunning shot,well done<br/></td>', 'stunning shot,well done', '2007-09-15 16:33:24.000000', NULL, 0),
